17.7 Proposal preconditions

Every proposal binds to:
- project revision;
- prompt instruction identity;
- prompt-body hash;
- response-contract hash;
- context signature;
- scope hash;
- prompt-engine version where applicable;
- referenced-record hashes;
- current response schema;
- Test IR runtime version where applicable.

Acceptance recomputes every precondition.
Reaccepting the same canonical envelope and scope returns existing identities and receipts and creates no duplicate state.

17.8 Extraction manifest

Every accepted agent value and relationship maps to:
- exact raw response;
- raw-response hash;
- exact JSON pointer with real array index;
- controlling prompt;
- prompt body hash;
- response-contract hash;
- context signature;
- raw-value hash;
- normalizer;
- normalized value;
- response temporary key;
- canonical collection;
- canonical record;
- canonical field or relationship;
- relationship target;
- evidence;
- validation rules;
- validation results;
- project revision;
- commit sequence;
- device timestamp.

Application-created IDs are recorded as application allocations, not falsely attributed to nonexistent response fields.

